1829	/// Builds the argv array for the process we should exec for the
1830	/// configured command. This isn't as straightforward as it seems since
1831	/// we deal with shell-wrapping, macOS login shells, etc.
1832	///
1833	/// The passwdpkg comptime argument is expected to have a single function
1834	/// `get(Allocator)` that returns a passwd entry. This is used by macOS
1835	/// to determine the username and home directory for the login shell.
1836	/// It is unused on other platforms.
1837	///
1838	/// Memory ownership:
1839	///
1840	/// The allocator should be an arena, since the returned value may or
1841	/// may not be allocated and args may or may not be allocated (or copied).
1842	/// Pointers in the return value may point to pointers in the command
1843	/// struct.

1305	pub const ReadThread = struct {
